WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.240
The highly anticipated release of James Gunn's
half-sequel, half-reboot The Suicide Squad

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:11.530
has wowed audiences and critics alike, earning
the movie a 91% Certified Fresh rating on

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.200
Rotten Tomatoes.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.320
Gunn's movie delivers on its promise of intense
R-rated violence and off-kilter humor, with

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:22.030
a cast that includes returning DC stalwarts
and a whole host of new squad members.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:27.030
The 2021 film finds Amanda Waller leading
two teams of crazy criminals to take down

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:31.940
a Nazi-era laboratory called Jötunheim, which
is rumored to be the home base of a secret

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.329
experiment known as "Project Starfish."

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:36.469
"We're all gonna die."

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.079
"I hope so."

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:39.719
"Oh, for God's sake."

00:00:39.719 --> 00:00:44.420
Following the critical disaster that was 2016's
Suicide Squad, there seemed to be nowhere

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:45.469
to go but up.

00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:49.729
The original film was highly profitable, but
maybe this time they could make a movie most

00:00:49.729 --> 00:00:51.109
people actually liked.

00:00:51.109 --> 00:00:55.449
The good news for film fans is, The Suicide
Squad appears to have succeeded when it comes

00:00:55.449 --> 00:00:58.889
to quality, winning over audiences and critics
alike.

00:00:58.889 --> 00:01:02.960
The bad news is, this one doesn't seem to
be making any money — or at least nowhere

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.740
near as much money as the 2016 one did.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:11.570
During its first weekend, the new movie made
approximately $26.5 million at the domestic

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:16.240
box office, falling short of expectations
that predicted it making at least $30 million

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:17.760
at the start.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.030
So what happened?

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:23.710
According to box office analysts, the rise
in the Delta variant of COVID-19 is likely

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:29.170
the most significant factor in why The Suicide
Squad fell short of its projected box office

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:30.170
return.

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:33.700
While the beginning of the summer saw many
businesses reopening, states relaxing their

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:38.450
mask guidelines, and daily life returning
to some form of normalcy, all that has been

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:43.079
challenged recently by media coverage of the
contagious COVID-19 variant.

00:01:43.079 --> 00:01:50.159
According to data from UC Davis Health, as
of July 22nd, 2021, almost 80% of the organization's

00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:55.229
COVID patients had the Delta variant, while
the CDC reported a higher percentage at the

00:01:55.229 --> 00:01:56.229
same time.

00:01:56.229 --> 00:02:01.010
The rise in the Delta variant has caused the
CDC and many businesses to revert to previous

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:05.749
mask and safety guidelines, suggesting that
people need to be more careful about the possible

00:02:05.749 --> 00:02:08.620
spread of the virus through indoor activities.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:13.110
This likely led many to postpone any plans
to visit a movie theater, considering the

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:16.530
high rate of transmission often found in that
environment.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:21.020
While it's unclear exactly how much the Delta
variant contributed to The Suicide Squad's

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:24.230
box office shortcomings, it was clearly an
influence.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:28.820
One of the other main reasons for Hollywood's
lower box office returns in 2021 has been

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:31.560
the shift from theatrical releases to streaming.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.890
Like every other recent Warner Bros. release,
The Suicide Squad was released simultaneously

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:38.590
in theaters and on HBO Max.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:42.611
Over the last year or so, that streaming platform
has given people who are unable to go to the

00:02:42.611 --> 00:02:47.650
theater a chance to catch the latest big releases
from the comfort of their own home.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:52.060
Other companies, such as Walt Disney Studios,
are also using a mixed theatrical and digital

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:56.040
release system, though it's unclear how this
will change going forward — and whether

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.290
it's financially sustainable for the studios
themselves.

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:03.180
Because of this recent trend, as well as the
ongoing shift over the past decade to more

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:07.490
streamable content, it's no longer possible
to rely on the box office as the best way

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:10.050
to measure the success of a new release.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:13.700
Even streaming figures are a little up in
the air: for example, the analytics company

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:19.440
Samba TV has suggested that around 2.8 million
U.S. households watched The Suicide Squad

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:24.160
on HBO Max on opening weekend, but it's difficult
to work out how that might have translated

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:28.390
into ticket sales, considering a household
can contain multiple people.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:32.040
Nonetheless, Deadline reports that the movie
at least holds the distinction of having the

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:37.390
top-grossing R-rated opening for a movie in
the pandemic era, but that may be a cold comfort

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:41.900
when comparing the receipts to the movie's
$185 million budget.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:46.200
With so many mixed signals, it's hard to argue
that The Suicide Squad is a bona fide box

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:49.780
office flop, even after you consider those
low returns.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:52.320
But it doesn't appear to have been a roaring
success, either.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.800
At the very least, the movie's a good one
— we can give them a hand for that.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.400
"Hand."

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.230
"Yes, that is your hand.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:00.790
Very good."

